; Match a phrase record to a command and find its objects
;
; Takes the parsed sentence at IY and prepares everything the check and the
; verb handlers need: FirstObject and SecondObject start as NO_OBJECT; the
; record workspace is cleared (#R$79A9); MatchCommand finds the command table
; record that fits the verb and prepositions (Z here: nothing fits and a message
; has been printed). The record's number (1-59) becomes CommandId and its
; address goes to RecPtr3. The flags of the command are unpacked (#R$7B78) and
; the scan for the first noun is set up (#R$7AA1). ActionPerform is set to 0
; (test pass).
; .
; A command with no nouns (bits 2-3 of StateB71D clear) is ready. For the
; others #R$7A14 finds the objects the noun phrases mean and puts them in
; FirstObject and SecondObject; if it cannot, #R$7DBC prints why (I see nothing
; to ..., or asks what is meant) and the sentence ends there. When ALL was typed
; (RecWork4 holds the ALL flag; it is copied to VerbAllFlag) the objects come one
; by one, once per call: an object that EXCEPT names is passed over (#R$7A73)
; and the scan carries on at the next one.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; IY Parsed phrase record
; O:F NZ when the sentence is matched and its objects are found, Z when it
; is not (the message is already printed)
; O:IX Command table record
@label=MatchSentence
c$79B6 LD A,$FF      ;
 $79B8 LD ($B6E9),A  ; SecondObject: none
 $79BB LD ($B6E8),A  ; FirstObject: none
 $79BE CALL $79A9    ; ResetRecWork
 $79C1 CALL $7B9E    ; MatchCommand
 $79C4 RET Z         ; no command fits
 $79C5 LD A,$01      ; A: the record's index in CommandTable, from 1
 $79C7 PUSH IX       ;
 $79C9 POP HL        ;
 $79CA LD DE,$AB53   ; CommandTable
 $79CD SBC HL,DE     ;
 $79CF JR Z,$79D9    ;
@isub=LD DE,COMMAND_RECORD_SIZE
 $79D1 LD DE,$0008   ;
*$79D4 INC A         ;
 $79D5 SBC HL,DE     ;
 $79D7 JR NZ,$79D4   ;
*$79D9 LD ($B6E7),A  ; CommandId
 $79DC LD ($B6E6),A  ; SavedCommandId
 $79DF LD ($795E),IX ; RecPtr3
 $79E3 CALL $7B78    ; UnpackFlags
 $79E6 CALL $7AA1    ; StartNounScan1
 $79E9 XOR A         ;
 $79EA LD ($B6FA),A  ; ActionPerform: test pass
 $79ED LD A,($B71D)  ; StateB71D: command flags
 $79F0 AND $0C       ; does the command take nouns?
 $79F2 JR Z,$7A11    ; no
 $79F4 LD A,($7952)  ; RecWork4: the ALL flag of the first word
 $79F7 LD ($B71C),A  ; VerbAllFlag
 $79FA RLCA          ;
 $79FB AND $01       ;
 $79FD LD ($7953),A  ; RecWork5: 1 when ALL
@label=MatchSentence_Object
*$7A00 CALL $7A14    ; ResolveNouns
 $7A03 JP NZ,$7DBC   ; no (or no single) object: say so
 $7A06 LD A,($B71C)  ; VerbAllFlag
 $7A09 AND A         ;
 $7A0A JR Z,$7A11    ; not ALL: done
 $7A0C CALL $7A73    ; IsExcluded: EXCEPT names this object?
 $7A0F JR NZ,$7A00   ; yes: take the next object
*$7A11 OR $01        ;
 $7A13 RET           ; NZ
